# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and credentials
#
# Nothing of this kind is in the repository or its history -- this section is
# a guard, not a cleanup. It is first because it is the only category here
# whose cost is not recoverable: a build artefact committed by accident is a
# `git rm` away, but a credential that reaches a public remote is burned the
# moment it is pushed and has to be rotated, not deleted.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.envrc
.direnv/
secrets.*
*.secret
*.secrets

# Credential files for the tools this project actually uses. `.pypirc` matters
# most now that releases go to PyPI: it is where an API token would live if
# anyone uploaded by hand. Releases use Trusted Publishing precisely so no such
# token needs to exist -- see docs/RELEASING.md.
.pypirc
.netrc
_netrc
.npmrc

# Key material and certificates.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
id_rsa
id_rsa.*
id_dsa
id_dsa.*
id_ecdsa
id_ecdsa.*
id_ed25519
id_ed25519.*
*.gpg
*.asc

# Cloud and CI credentials that land in a working tree by accident.
.aws/
gha-creds-*.json
service-account*.json

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local tool state
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Claude Code local state (push counter, last checkpoint SHA) -- per-checkout,
# never shared. This must stay ignored: if the counter file entered the repo,
# every push's measured size would be inflated by the counter's own diff.
.claude/state/

# Per-developer permission grants. `.claude/settings.json` IS tracked, because
# it registers the push-counter hook the whole project depends on; the .local
# variant is personal and must not be.
.claude/settings.local.json

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
pip-wheel-metadata/

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
ENV/
env/

# Testing / tooling caches
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.hypothesis/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
.tox/
.nox/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated by docfix itself
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Output from local runs and tests. docfix never writes over its input, so
# these are always new files sitting beside the source.
*.formatted.md
*.formatted.docx
*.formatted.pdf

# The pinned font cache normally lives in the user cache directory, but
# DOCFIX_FONT_CACHE can point anywhere -- including here. The repo ships no
# font binaries and should not start now.
/fonts-cache/
/.docfix-fonts/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors and operating systems
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.iml
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# Logs and scratch
*.log
